  "id": "mating-behavior",
  "term": "mating behavior",
  "definition": "Mating behavior is the set of actions and sensory processes involved in achieving copulation and remating. In the studied species, it included reliance on vision, physical contact such as the male’s foretarsi, and patterns of repeated mating that affected reproductive success.",
